***************************
* SET UP THE INITIAL DATA *
***************************

NAME          LUKSAN22LC

*   Problem :
*   *********

*   Problem 22 (attracting-repelling) in the paper

*     L. Luksan
*     Hybrid methods in large sparse nonlinear least squares
*     J. Optimization Theory & Applications 89(3) 575-595 (1996)

*   SIF input: Nick Gould, June 2017.
*   Modified version of LUKSAN22LS (formulation corrected), Pim Heeman, June 2026.
*   Updated to improve processing, Pim Heeman, May 2026.

*   least-squares version

*   classification SUR2-AN-V-0

*   The version LUKSAN22LS had a numerical value misaligned
*   such that the first part would get cut off.

*  number of unknowns

 IE N                   100

*  number of equations

 IM M         N         2
 IA M         M         -2

*   Define useful parameters

 IE 1                   1
 IE 2                   2
 IA N-1       N         -1
 IA N-2       N         -2

VARIABLES

 DO I         1                        N
 X  X(I)
 ND

GROUPS

 N  E1        X1        1.0
 IE K                   2
 DO I         1                        N-2
 IA I+1       I         1
 IA K+1       K         1
 XN E(K)      X(I+1)    -10.0
 XN E(K+1)
 IA K         K         2
 ND
 XN E(K)      X(N)      -10.0

CONSTANTS

 X  LUKSAN22C E1        1.0

BOUNDS

 FR LUKSAN22C 'DEFAULT'

START POINT

 DO I         1                        N
 DI I         2
 IA I+1       I         1
 XV LUKSAN22C X(I)       -1.2
 XV LUKSAN22C X(I+1)     1.0
 ND

ELEMENT TYPE

 EV SQR       X
 EV EXPDA     X1
 EV EXPDA     X2
 IV EXPDA     X
 EV EXPDB     X1
 EV EXPDB     X2
 IV EXPDB     X

ELEMENT USES

 IE K                   2
 DO I         1                        N-2
 IA I+1       I         1
 IA I+2       I         2
 IA K+1       K         1
 XT E(K)      SQR
 ZV E(K)      X                        X(I)
 XT E(K+1)    EXPDA
 ZV E(K+1)    X1                       X(I)
 ZV E(K+1)    X2                       X(I+1)
 XT F(K+1)    EXPDB
 ZV F(K+1)    X1                       X(I+1)
 ZV F(K+1)    X2                       X(I+2)
 IA K         K         2
 ND
 XT E(K)      SQR
 ZV E(K)      X                        X(N-1)

GROUP TYPE

 GV L2        GVAR

GROUP USES

 XT 'DEFAULT' L2

 IE K                   2
 DO I         1                        N-2
 IA K+1       K         1
 XE E(K)      E(K)      10.0
 XE E(K+1)    E(K+1)                   F(K+1)
 IA K         K         2
 ND
 XE E(K)      E(K)      10.0

OBJECT BOUND

 LO LUKSAN22C            0.0

*   Solution

*LO SOLTN                0.0

ENDATA

***********************
* SET UP THE FUNCTION *
* AND RANGE ROUTINES  *
***********************

ELEMENTS      LUKSAN22LC

TEMPORARIES

 M  EXP
 R  EXPARG

INDIVIDUALS

 T  SQR
 F                      X * X
 G  X                   X + X
 H  X         X         2.0D0

 T  EXPDA
 R  X         X1        1.0            X2        -1.0
 A  EXPARG              2.0D0 * EXP( - X * X )
 F                      EXPARG
 G  X                   - 2.0D0 * X * EXPARG
 H  X         X         ( 4.0D0 * X * X - 2.0D0 ) * EXPARG

 T  EXPDB
 R  X         X1        1.0            X2        -1.0
 A  EXPARG              EXP( - 2.0D0 * X * X )
 F                      EXPARG
 G  X                   - 4.0D0 * X * EXPARG
 H  X         X         ( 16.0D0 * X * X - 4.0D0 ) * EXPARG

ENDATA

*********************
* SET UP THE GROUPS *
* ROUTINE           *
*********************

GROUPS        LUKSAN22LC

INDIVIDUALS

 T  L2
 F                      GVAR * GVAR
 G                      GVAR + GVAR
 H                      2.0

ENDATA
